{
  "_comment": "Template for the CTO home's .claude/settings.json. Apply with scripts/cto/settings-posture.sh --apply (a merge: keeps your MCP servers, additionalDirectories and hooks). Do NOT include the _comment fields when applying; preflight.sh runs --check at every session start.",
  "_comment_posture": "PERMISSIONS POSTURE (CEO 2026-11-01): the conversation is the gate, the harness is lenient. The CEO approves a batch in the conversation ('yes, merge all the open PRs'), the CTO records it, and it runs with no per-command prompt. allow carries the blanket Bash so routine shepherding (peek, send, commit, push, reap, reviews) is silent. ask carries ONLY the never-uninvited set: what the CTO must not do without having asked first. deny > ask > allow in every scope regardless of specificity, so an ask rule prompts every time; 'don't ask again' cannot silence it (the allow it writes never wins) — remove the rule if a command stops being risky. Project-specific additions (object-store deletes, service installs) go in .cto/settings-overlay.json, not here.",
  "_comment_defaultMode": "acceptEdits is the posture: Edit/Write auto-approved, Bash covered by the blanket allow below, ask-listed commands prompt (forwarded by Remote Control; /config 'Push when actions required' pings the phone). AUTO mode drops the blanket Bash allow on entry and judges every call with a classifier whose block is NOT a prompt — fine for unattended runs, wrong for a session the CEO is approving things in. Shift+Tab cycles default -> acceptEdits -> plan (-> auto if enabled); bypassPermissions is not in the cycle unless the session was launched with it.",
  "defaultMode": "acceptEdits",
  "_comment_harnessTools": "Monitor / TaskStop / PushNotification are HARNESS-NATIVE tools, not Bash — the Bash rule does not cover them, so without these entries the orchestrator prompts on every watcher arm. Monitor is also the sanctioned way to run a watcher past the background-Bash cap; see scripts/cto/watch-file-or-prompt.sh --stream for what it should wrap.",
  "_comment_opsScripts": "The blanket Bash covers scripts/cto/*.sh, so ops scripts need no per-script allow entries. If you ever narrow it, write absolute-path prefix rules (\"Bash(bash /path/to/home/scripts/cto/<script>.sh *)\"); variable expansion inside permission rules is not documented and must not be relied on.",
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash",
      "Edit",
      "Write",
      "Read",
      "Glob",
      "Grep",
      "WebFetch",
      "WebSearch",
      "mcp__domshell__domshell_execute",
      "Monitor",
      "TaskStop",
      "PushNotification"
    ],
    "_comment_ask": "The never-uninvited set. Rewriting remote history, deleting remote branches, launchd persistence, creating/deleting/re-scoping GitHub repos, and the CTO editing its own permission files. Each prompts once per use, in every mode, including auto. Merges, pushes, commits, worktree reaps are NOT here: the CEO approves those in the conversation.",
    "ask": [
      "Bash(git push --force*)",
      "Bash(git push -f *)",
      "Bash(git push * --force*)",
      "Bash(git push * -f *)",
      "Bash(git push --delete *)",
      "Bash(git push * --delete *)",
      "Bash(git push * -d *)",
      "Bash(git branch -D *)",
      "Bash(launchctl load *)",
      "Bash(launchctl unload *)",
      "Bash(launchctl bootstrap *)",
      "Bash(launchctl bootout *)",
      "Bash(gh repo create *)",
      "Bash(gh repo delete *)",
      "Bash(gh repo edit *)",
      "Edit(.claude/settings.json)",
      "Edit(.claude/settings.local.json)",
      "Write(.claude/settings.json)",
      "Write(.claude/settings.local.json)",
      "Edit(~/.claude/settings.json)",
      "Write(~/.claude/settings.json)"
    ]
  },
  "_comment_skillBudget": "Default skill listing budget is 1% of context. With ~15 skills planned, raise to 2% to keep descriptions intact.",
  "skillListingBudgetFraction": 0.02,
  "hooks": {
    "_comment_SessionStart": "Run preflight on every session start. Output appears in Claude's context as additionalContext — warnings/errors surface immediately. It also reads the hook input's permission_mode and reports it.",
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/agentic/preflight.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "_comment_Stop_inbox": "Drain ~/.cto/inbox/ at the end of every turn. Sprint B work — wire this in once /escalate-drain skill exists.",
    "_Stop_placeholder": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/agentic/inbox-peek.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/deny-authorization-forge.sh"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/deny-authorization-forge.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "_comment_PreToolUse": "deny-authorization-forge: allows a CTO-home session (it records the CEO's words, record-approval.sh); denies dev lanes writing CEO-AUTHORIZATION.md (CEO ruling 2026-10-30)."
  }
}
